/* LowerBound_r: intermediate level of LowerBound, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the
   component BART refines.
   Purpose: replace min({kk | ...} \/ {max_IDX + 1}) by the three facts a loop establishes: the
   result is a position or max_IDX + 1, every position before it is below value, and it is at least
   value if it is a position. The proof that these facts define the minimum is thus done once, here,
   away from the loop, and needs no order on the array. Same shape as FindArray_r of the find-array
   demonstration.
   The precondition is repeated in full: the order on the array is what the binary search of the
   next step relies on, and only there. */
REFINEMENT
    LowerBound_r

REFINES
    LowerBound

SEES
    Ctx_LowerBound

OPERATIONS

    pos <-- lower_bound(array, value) =
    PRE
        array : (0..max_IDX) --> INT &
        value : INT &
        !(ii, jj).(ii : 0..max_IDX & jj : 0..max_IDX & ii <= jj => array(ii) <= array(jj))
    THEN
        pos :( pos : 0..max_IDX + 1 &
               !ii.(ii : 0..pos - 1 => array(ii) < value) &
               (pos <= max_IDX => value <= array(pos)) )
    END

END
